  "notes": "The last composition class: ice crown x MO size tail. Measured: the _DEEP arm's _MO_PMF already prints a sweep footprint ~11x the tape's (p_ge2 ~0.5 vs 0.045) and yet the emptied-touch channel stays ~1% \u2014 sweep width is not the binding constraint. Iceberg reload fires per consumed unit, so ANY mid-burst reload keeps the level alive no matter how deep the burst cuts. The residual sharpens again: hidden persistence must be per-level (reload gated on the burst ending / residual visible depth), not per-unit.",
